  Which behaviour does the lane depend on? `remedy = is_covered and not is_live` for DEADPOINTER — settlement of a dead-pointer mismatch requires BOTH the appended correction row naming (DEADPOINTER, surface) AND the referenced R68-M<n> row actually existing in LOG.md/corpus/lessons/round-{68,69}.md. Ca2's predicate ("unannotated_mismatches=0", MISMATCHES leg) is only trustworthy because this conjunct exists; without it, the lane could "pass" Ca2 by appending a row while the fleet report still points at a mistake row that exists nowhere — a fabricated-settlement class. Also worth noting the symmetrical observation: for the L1's real integration, the remedy must actually land the M9 row (e.g. in corpus/lessons/round-69.md `## Mistakes` or LOG) — the counter will verify it.

